<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Fat Lady Trail and Fat Lady Saddle (from Pocket Creek Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:205-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:pocket-creek-sno-park (OSM node 6287637025); confidence: high; pdf_page: 206; book_elev_ft: 3800; quote: From Pocket Creek Sno-Park, 13 miles around Hood from Government Camp, ski east on the almost level road 0.6 mile to a bridge crossing of the East Fork</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302220" lon="-121.603446"><ele>1288.4</ele><name>Upper Junction</name><desc>source: as in or-vielbig-2e_204-1: OSM junction of Forest Road 3540 and Forest Road 3540-640; DEM 4,227 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 206; book_elev_ft: 4200; quote: to a road junction, hereafter referred to as the "Upper Junction," 2.7 miles from the trailhead</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.295170" lon="-121.593280"><ele>1428.4</ele><name>Mount Adams view clearcut (Fat Lady Trail turnoff)</name><desc>source: OSM node 3713226242, junction of Forest Road 3540-640 and Forest Road 3540-641 (the logging side road that climbs back south); 1.36 mi along 640 from the Upper Junction; DEM 4,686 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 208; book_elev_ft: 4640; quote: from the Upper Junction ski upward 1.3 miles on the upper Pocket Creek road to the Mount Adams view clearcut at 4,640 feet ... Here, a logging side road (Fat Lady Trail) turns off and climbs back up going southward</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.287480" lon="-121.594600"><ele>1530.2</ele><name>Foot of the talus slope</name><desc>source: OSM node 3713226260 on Forest Road 3540-641, 0.55 mi up from the turnoff; DEM 5,020 ft (the book's 620 ft climb would put the foot at 4,900 ft, 0.38 mi up); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 208; quote: ski the Fat Lady Trail 0.6 mile up from the Mount Adams view clearcut to where a steep snowfield appears through the trees to the left (east). This is a summer rock slide.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.286600" lon="-121.592200"><ele>1588.4</ele><name>Top of the open slope</name><desc>source: placed east of the road, on the left side of the slope below the saddle, from the DEM grid (about 5,220 ft); confidence: low; pdf_page: 208; quote: Climb up the left side of the open slope and switchback up through the old growth</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.285090" lon="-121.590530"><ele>1682.4</ele><name>Fat Lady Saddle</name><desc>source: DEM col between the 5,680+ ft peak at 45.2840,-121.5948 (the map's 5724 pyramid) and the ridge running north-east; OSM Gunsight Trail #685 node 3669713822 crosses it; DEM 5,520 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 207; book_elev_ft: 5520; quote: Fat Lady Saddle (5,520 feet) is east of the trail and at the north foot of a pyramid-shaped high point on Gunsight Ridge at the head of Pocket Creek</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Fat Lady Trail and Fat Lady Saddle (from Pocket Creek Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Pocket Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Upper Junction: osm (high), 2.66 mi | 2. Upper Junction -&gt; Mount Adams view clearcut (Fat Lady Trail turnoff): osm (high), 1.32 mi | 3. Mount Adams view clearcut (Fat Lady Trail turnoff) -&gt; Foot of the talus slope: osm (high), 0.55 mi | 4. Foot of the talus slope -&gt; Top of the open slope: straight (low), 0.13 mi | 5. Top of the open slope -&gt; Fat Lady Saddle: straight (low), 0.13 mi</desc>
